# {{ name }}

> TODO: Describe what this web app does.

React 19 + Vite + TypeScript SPA, generated from the `react-web` template.

## Tech Stack

- **React 19** + **TypeScript**, built with **Vite**
- **TanStack Query** for server state, **React Router** for routing
- **Vitest** + **Testing Library** for tests, **ESLint** for linting

## Commands

Run from the repository root:

| Command | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `make dev APP={{ name }}` | Vite dev server on http://localhost:3000 |
| `make run APP={{ name }} TASK=test` | Run tests |
| `make run APP={{ name }} TASK=lint` | Lint |
| `make run APP={{ name }} TASK=typecheck` | Type-check |
| `make run APP={{ name }} TASK=build` | Production build to `dist/` |
| `make up` | Run in Docker Compose (unprivileged nginx, port {{ port }}) |

## Calling the API

The app calls the backend at `/api` on its own origin:

- **Dev**: Vite proxies `/api/*` to `http://localhost:8080` (see `vite.config.ts`)
- **Docker**: nginx proxies `/api/*` to `API_UPSTREAM` (default `{{ api_upstream }}`)

Set `VITE_API_URL` at build time only if the API is on a different origin.

## Structure

Features are collocated under `src/features/<feature>/` with `components/`, `hooks/`,
`services/` and `types/`. Shared UI lives in `src/shared/`.

## Releases

Versioned independently by Release Please. Use the `{{ name }}` scope in commits,
e.g. `feat({{ name }}): add orders page`.
